WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:20.434
"Hear me! This is an order from the sultan!" shouted one of the sultan's men.

2
00:00:20.435 --> 00:00:24.193
"Cover your windows and close your doors.

3
00:00:24.194 --> 00:00:30.003
Princess Badra will pass through these streets today to go to the bathhouse.

4
00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:32.746
No one must look upon her!

5
00:00:32.747 --> 00:00:38.387
Whoever does not obey this order will be killed!"

6
00:00:38.388 --> 00:00:41.623
Did Aladdin run home when he heard these words?

7
00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:44.662
No, he did not.

8
00:00:44.663 --> 00:00:48.221
"Princess Badra," he sighed.

9
00:00:48.222 --> 00:00:52.034
"Everyone thinks she must be very lovely."

10
00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:56.530
It was true. She was very beautiful.

11
00:00:56.531 --> 00:01:00.494
But only a few people had ever seen her face.

12
00:01:00.495 --> 00:01:05.856
Whenever Princess Badra left the palace, she always wore a veil.

13
00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:11.720
And every one of her visits to this bathhouse caused excitement.

14
00:01:11.721 --> 00:01:17.029
"Get off the street, you people!" yelled one man in a red cap.

15
00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.261
"Go home!" shouted an old woman.

16
00:01:20.262 --> 00:01:23.288
"Or hide in your shops!"

17
00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:29.460
Aladdin stood in the street as the merchants and shoppers pushed past him.

18
00:01:29.461 --> 00:01:33.926
"I must see the face of the princess," Aladdin decided.

19
00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:38.556
"I've heard her eyes are deep and dark like the night sky."

20
00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:42.564
Soon Aladdin was the only one left in the street.

21
00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:47.677
Suddenly he heard the sound of flutes from around a corner.

22
00:01:47.678 --> 00:01:50.839
"It must be the princess and her attendants," said Aladdin.

23
00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.394
"I must hurry."

24
00:01:52.395 --> 00:01:56.669
He ran inside the bathhouse and quickly hid behind a door.

25
00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.562
He was just in time.

26
00:01:59.563 --> 00:02:06.587
Aladdin heard voices now, and one voice was sweeter than all the others.

27
00:02:06.588 --> 00:02:12.994
"How lovely it will be to relax in the hot steam," sighed the voice.

28
00:02:12.995 --> 00:02:18.834
As the princess entered the bathhouse, Aladdin peeked out from behind the door.

29
00:02:18.835 --> 00:02:25.570
Just then Princess Badra removed the veil from her face.

30
00:02:25.571 --> 00:02:28.975
"Oh my!" whispered Aladdin.

31
00:02:28.976 --> 00:02:35.223
Aladdin saw her deep, dark eyes and her smiling, red mouth.

32
00:02:35.224 --> 00:02:37.021
He could not breathe.

33
00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:39.110
He could not move!

34
00:02:39.111 --> 00:02:47.972
"I know nothing of beauty," he thought, "but I know Princess Badra must be the most beautiful girl in the world."

35
00:02:47.973 --> 00:02:53.021
In one moment, he had fallen in love with the sultan's daughter.

36
00:02:53.022 --> 00:02:59.672
No one saw Aladdin as he left the bathhouse through a back door.

37
00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:05.964
When he returned home, his mother said, "Back so soon?"

38
00:03:05.965 --> 00:03:07.903
Aladdin did not answer.

39
00:03:07.904 --> 00:03:12.593
He sat down on a cushion and stared into space.

40
00:03:12.594 --> 00:03:15.757
"Eat something," Zeba said.

41
00:03:15.758 --> 00:03:18.870
She set some bread and dried fruits before him.

42
00:03:18.871 --> 00:03:21.627
"You don't look well."

43
00:03:21.628 --> 00:03:28.098
She poured him a cup of strong coffee, but Aladdin still did not say a word.

44
00:03:28.099 --> 00:03:31.738
"What has happened to you?" she asked.

45
00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:35.033
"Why won't you speak to me?"

46
00:03:35.034 --> 00:03:39.846
"Please, leave me alone," Aladdin answered.

47
00:03:39.847 --> 00:03:43.172
He ate a bite of bread and then went to his room.

48
00:03:43.173 --> 00:03:46.631
He lay awake all night.

49
00:03:46.632 --> 00:03:50.916
Morning came, but Aladdin still did not move.

50
00:03:50.917 --> 00:03:52.707
Zeba was worried.

51
00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:55.459
"Are you in pain?" she said.

52
00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.295
"Shall I get a doctor?"

53
00:03:58.296 --> 00:04:00.734
"I am not sick," he murmured.

54
00:04:00.735 --> 00:04:02.629
"I am in love."

55
00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:06.848
"In love!" cried his mother with delight.

56
00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:08.604
"Oh, my son!

57
00:04:08.605 --> 00:04:10.418
Who is this lucky lady?

58
00:04:10.419 --> 00:04:13.231
Tell me quickly!"

59
00:04:13.232 --> 00:04:18.222
"I am in love with Princess Badra," said Aladdin calmly.

60
00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:20.668
"And I have decided to marry her."

61
00:04:20.669 --> 00:04:30.245
Aladdin's mother stared at him with surprise and then burst out laughing.

62
00:04:30.246 --> 00:04:33.226
"Marry the sultan's daughter?

63
00:04:33.227 --> 00:04:37.282
You? A tailor's son?"

64
00:04:37.283 --> 00:04:42.620
"Yes," said Aladdin quietly. "I will marry her."

65
00:04:42.621 --> 00:04:50.279
Zeba raised her hands over her head and cried out, "My son has lost his mind!

66
00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:57.303
The genies have made him crazy!"
